  "body": "Two cross-drill tests fail on `upstream/main` (cac115a), found while gating PR #149 (#127), which doesn't touch this code.\n\n**Platform:** macOS (Apple Silicon), debug build, `scripts/gate.sh quick` and plain `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test <suite>`. Not checked on Windows or Linux. If they pass there, this may be platform float sensitivity rather than a regression.\n\n### 1. `drilling_cross_box::a_cylinder_stock_chain_is_unchanged_bit_for_bit`\n\n```\npanicked at crates/app/tests/drilling_cross_box.rs:264:5:\nassertion `left == right` failed: the round-bar chains moved\n  left: [15691376060994952168, 10503253365309833769]\n right: [2202346499980779381, 1828336726059972913]\n```\nBoth pinned fingerprints differ (the three-hole chain and the off-centre hole on a Ø40 mill-turn bar).\n\n### 2. `drilling_cross_spindle::a_cross_drill_off_the_world_origin_under_a_moved_g54_drills_the_on_origin_chain`\n\n```\npanicked at crates/app/tests/drilling_cross_spindle.rs:173:9:\nassertion `left == right` failed: lathe: the same chain, move for move\n  left: 13\n right: 14\n```\nOn the lathe, the bar placed under a moved G54 produces one more move than the same bar at the origin. The post would output a different chain depending only on where the work offset sits, so this one may be more than a stale golden.\n\n### Possibly related\nThese are the latest commits to both test files; I haven't bisected:\n- 9a095b7 fix(app): read a cross hole's entry at the true round, part included\n- 3b974ea fix(app): enter a cross hole where its own line meets the stock\n- dd9dd41 fix(app): judge only axial lathe holes by the axial-hole verdict\n\n### Reproduce\n```\ngit switch --detach upstream/main\ncargo test -p camcraft-app --test drilling_cross_box --test drilling_cross_spindle --no-fail-fast\n```\n\n---\nFiled by an agent for an outside contributor (fork mkinney/Camcraft), who has no label rights here. Suggested labels: `bug`, `area:turning`, `source:agent`, and a priority (P1, or P0 if #2 is a real offset-dependent path change).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
